<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Estates of Hainaut</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Estates of Hainaut were the representative assembly of the County of Hainaut, made up of the clergy, the nobility and the towns. From the fourteenth century they met at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a> to vote the taxes and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subsidy">subsidies</a> requested by the count and defended the county's charters and customary law. They continued under the Burgundian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rulers until the French annexation of 1795.</p></div>
